1
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:15,957
Gyro Zeppeli wins!

2
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:20,660
We have our first race
leader on the Steel Ball Run!

3
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:30,460
He did it!

4
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,057
Gyro came in first.

5
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,457
The secret to his victory was...

6
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,620
the power of the spin!

7
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:39,640
Fine work today, Valkyrie.

8
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:44,637
I have to win this race, no matter
the cost, so give it your all.

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,580
No pressure, though, right?

10
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:49,100
Gyro Zeppeli.

11
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:53,300
That man does not volunteer
details of his past.

12
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:55,973
According to authorities, he's new here.

13
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:59,455
He came to America from Genoa,
Italy this last May, Mr.

14
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,370
Steele.

15
00:01:00,453 --> 00:01:01,283
Hmm?

16
00:01:01,366 --> 00:01:02,196
So he's a foreigner?

17
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:03,410
Yes, sir.

18
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:07,638
He arrived on a ship registered to
a certain Royal European bloodline.

19
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:09,600
Mr. Steele!

20
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,920
The deliberation results are in!

21
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:13,940
I don't get it.

22
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:16,240
This can't be happening!

23
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:21,160
Don't tell me my 1 in 5 billion
luck is coming gone already, man!

24
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:25,160
How could First Place have
eluded me? Damn it all!

25
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:27,060
I am D .O. Brando!

26
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,197
Would anyone like some food?

27
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,692
Our racers eat for free!

28
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,860
He looks like the registration clerk.

29
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:38,634
Is it a different guy?

30
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:40,960
I'll take it.

31
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,068
Just the way you called it.

32
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,458
You have my congratulations for now.

33
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,935
Thanks for that, kid.

34
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:56,934
But don't be too gracious in defeat,
unless you're throwing in the towel.

35
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:00,240
To one and all, I laud your patience.

36
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,337
The first stage rankings
will now be unveiled.

37
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:06,877
After much careful deliberation,
the winner of the first leg?

38
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:10,380
is the possessor of Saddlecloth 990!

39
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:11,740
It's Sandman!

40
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,397
Thank

41
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,797
you

42
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:58,880
so

43
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,830
much

44
00:03:05,913 --> 00:03:12,480
for

45
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:15,370
watching.

46
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,940
Let's go.

47
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:52,400
I will explain all.

48
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:55,425
Based on observations
from our hot air balloon,

49
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:58,577
Gyro Zeppeli used a weapon
to obstruct the path ahead.

50
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:02,337
It was at the end of the downhill
slope just before the final turn.

51
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,655
The end of the slope?

52
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:06,820
Oh, then.

53
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,620
As a result,

54
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:13,277
Gyro will be demoted 20 places
in this first leg of the race,

55
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:16,360
and the racers behind him
will move up accordingly.

56
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:19,240
So, Dio's second, huh?

57
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,580
And Poco Loco got third.

58
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:25,357
Yeah, but the big news here is
that Mountain Tim came in fourth.

59
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:28,675
He squeezed his horse's nose
in there right at the end.

60
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:31,642
Slow Dancer, what are you doing?

61
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:34,580
Mountain Tim?

62
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:38,000
A cowboy forged in the
crucible of the West.

63
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:40,822
I'd heard the rumors, of course?

64
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:44,477
That all horses bow their
heads in respect to him!

65
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,620
when he passes by.

66
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:56,737
Congratulations, Mr.

67
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:58,879
Steel, on a successful first stage.

68
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,180
Much obliged.

69
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:02,422
When will the next one commence?

70
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:20,317
Something you wish to get
off your chest, Zeppelin?

71
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:24,400
Normally you'd be disqualified for
that stunt you pulled back there.

72
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,080
No, sir, no complaints.

73
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,518
No point complaining about the past.

74
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:35,448
It's not like I can
take it back now, right?

75
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:36,470
Hmm.

76
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:41,040
Guess I came here, so I can head
into tomorrow on a fresh slate.

77
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,800
Enjoy your champagne.

78
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,240
I know I will.

79
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,860
Hey, what do you mean?

80
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,270
Whoa!

81
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:50,790
Huh?

82
00:05:50,873 --> 00:05:52,120
What in the...

83
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,420
What is the meaning of this?

84
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:01,267
I paid cop's dollar to
ship this into France!

85
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,080
Excuse me, sir.

86
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:14,530
Hmm?

87
00:06:14,613 --> 00:06:15,580
Problem, Sheriff?

88
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,817
May I have a moment of your time?

89
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:19,488
We should speak in private.

90
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:22,916
Is it wrong that made me feel better?

91
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:28,764
Are you going to nip at my heels in the
second stage of the race, Johnny Joe Star?

92
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:30,330
Well, yeah.

93
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,501
Right up until I breeze past you.

94
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:35,660
Very well.

95
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,620
Here is your second lesson.

96
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:40,660
Never let your muscles
in on the plan. Ever.

97
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:42,930
Observe.

98
00:06:43,013 --> 00:06:46,117
The more pressure you apply when
grabbing your wrist with your free hand,

99
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:50,200
the more your muscles want to react
to that force by shaking it off.

100
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:52,757
The body instinctively
tries to protect itself

101
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:55,217
because the muscles sense what's going on.

102
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:57,418
That's how it is with living bodies.

103
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:01,880
The steel ball's spin keeps them
in the dark, so keep it skin deep.

104
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:05,840
That way, the muscles have no
idea something strange is afoot.

105
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:07,580
Keep it skin-deep, huh?

106
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:08,937
That's your advice?

107
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,196
Give it a whirl, if you're up for it.

108
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:15,774
That champagne cork in your hand has
some pretty good spin going already.

109
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,836
And that's how you get off the horse.

110
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,178
Their muscles didn't even notice it.

111
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:38,148
That was the reverse of the spin
for when I got on the horse!

112
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,617
Keep the muscles in the dark.

113
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:44,524
It's not the steel ball itself,
but the power of spin that's key.

114
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:48,097
Stage two of the race crosses
the desert, Johnny Joestar.

115
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:50,060
Over 700 miles in total.

116
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,793
It's going to be tough.

117
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:54,380
I say we form an alliance.

118
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:58,268
What better way to finish the
stage than in first and second?

119
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:02,654
I'll be the one in first place, though.

120
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:06,810
What?

121
00:08:06,893 --> 00:08:08,660
What the hell am I looking at?

122
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,577
Pretty obvious, ain't it?

123
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:14,557
You're looking at the scene
of a brutal murder, sir.

124
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:17,680
A massacre carried out
during your steel ball run.

125
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:20,637
Over 3,000 racers took
part in that first leg of

126
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:23,577
the race and not a damn
one of them saw anything.

127
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:25,440
You think it was a jockey?

128
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:27,077
But what motive would they have to...

129
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:29,377
I can think of a cool 50 million of them.

130
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:32,107
For that much money,
nothing's off the table.

131
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:35,077
All participants are
suspects at this juncture,

132
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,737
and we must assume there
will be more victims.

133
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:41,644
Do you intend to halt the race to
allow for a full investigation?

134
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:44,470
No!

135
00:08:44,553 --> 00:08:48,440
The steel ball run is bigger
than any one man's ambitions now!

136
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,420
I figured as much.

137
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,880
Please, dear.

138
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,060
Be careful.

139
00:08:57,780 --> 00:09:00,780
The scent of these blooms
is said to calm the soul.

140
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:04,937
I would be honored if
you would accept them.

141
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:11,577
I'm sure you're

142
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:12,490
worried sick

143
00:09:12,573 --> 00:09:13,403
for your beloved husband.

144
00:09:13,486 --> 00:09:15,437
Man, what life wouldn't be.

145
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,957
I'll sort this out finer than frog hair.

146
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:22,397
That's mountain.

147
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,497
Tim is it not?

148
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:24,977
What's he doing here?

149
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:27,577
I brought him out to
track down the killer.

150
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:29,297
It's right in his wheelhouses.

151
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:30,439
I'm sure you know?

152
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:31,937
Track down the killer?

153
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,785
But he's a member of the race.

154
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,257
All the more reason to you.

155
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:38,277
Next, what better motivation
to catch the culprit quick?

156
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,600
I'm touched by your concern. Mr.

157
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:44,720
Steel, I'm appointing Mountain Tim
as deputy sheriff in this matter.

158
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:47,864
If and that meets with
your approval, of course.

159
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,880
A hell of a way to go.

160
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:57,262
How am I supposed to win the race in peace,
knowing it contained so vile a villain?

161
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:02,304
I got a lot of friends in the race and
I'll be damned if I let them get butchered.

162
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:09,441
If I have to pick a set of prints
to start tracking, it's this one!

163
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:13,280
You gotta run a horse hard
to get prints like this.

164
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:16,977
And there's a mountain-shaped ship
in the middle of this horseshoe?

165
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:18,100
What of it?

166
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:22,677
Bet you this horse was riled up,
probably from seeing all that carnage.

167
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:25,777
But the rider kept him under
control during the murder.

168
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:29,460
They know the terrain a
bottle near the victims.

169
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:35,880
Something solid inside there
is that a close button.

170
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:45,277
Does it have something to
do with how they met their

171
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:48,419
grizzly end it came off of
one of the victims jeans?

172
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:53,849
Why would the button be off though, and
how did it end up inside that bottle?

173
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:55,700
In any case,

174
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:58,217
by the time our killer
got close enough that

175
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:00,397
these poor unfortunates
took stock of them,

176
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,421
it was too late.

177
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:14,200
Five minutes until the starting gun.

178
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:19,180
The second stage is Herculean,
covering some 750 miles in total.

179
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:22,345
It will be the work of
two weeks, give or take.

180
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:27,582
The racers will brave the deserts of Arizona,
reaching the goal in Monument Valley.

181
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:30,477
So long as they pass through
our mandated checkpoint,

182
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:33,795
they are free to choose their
own routes along the way.

183
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:34,750
Gyro,

184
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:36,617
the paper says Sandman
is the favorite to win

185
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,577
this betting and he's
the odds on favorite.

186
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:40,380
What do you think? Not me.

187
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:42,397
There's no accounting for taste.

188
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,077
Clearly they're missing out.

189
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:46,217
Did you know I'm the sixth most popular?

190
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:48,097
It says here that you're ninth.

191
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:49,500
Pearls before swine.

192
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,817
They wouldn't know talent.

193
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:52,460
if I spun it up their ass.

194
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:54,408
Not that I care, of course.

195
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,967
See Mountain Tim over there?

196
00:11:57,260 --> 00:12:00,201
He's popular with the fans
and favored to win too.

197
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,740
Easy there, boy.

198
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:03,640
He's got a weird hat.

199
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:06,460
Just look, I kind of want to trample it.

200
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,897
Bearing it if I'm being completely on it.

201
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:10,980
Mountain Tim is a bonafide cowboy.

202
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,157
Short stages aren't
supposed to be his strength!

203
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,937
but he still caught up with
me without my noticing it.

204
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:18,137
and passed me right at the finish line.

205
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:20,377
Even with that hat of
his, you didn't see him?

206
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,872
Kind of beggar's belief.

207
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:28,781
Looking over a map of the area, I think our
biggest challenge will be finding water.

208
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:33,760
All 26 members of a cavalry
unit died out there in 1875.

209
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:37,540
It wasn't a battle or an
accident that did them in.

210
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,395
A watering hole there for some reason.

211
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:43,777
They searched in vain for
another source of hydration.

212
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:46,507
The burning sun beating
the life out of them.

213
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,440
But it was no use.

214
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,169
They all roasted to death.

215
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:52,110
Magic.

216
00:12:52,193 --> 00:12:54,080
The map says there's water here,

217
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,377
30 miles out from where we start?

218
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,757
and the only one that day.

219
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:02,369
If we can't find it along the way, we'll
be too dead to worry about the race.

220
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:07,960
Also, this cork, what do I
have to do to spin this thing?

221
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:12,657
Our racers gather at the line,

222
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:15,916
ready to face the next of
their levers with daring do.

223
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:22,540
And they're up, the second stage of
the Steel Ball Run has commenced!

224
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,410
Huh?

225
00:13:24,493 --> 00:13:28,720
I'll be damned, Gyro Zeppeli searches
ahead to claim an early lead!

226
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:32,240
Is he stubborn as a mule or just an idiot?

227
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:35,522
When I warned him earlier,
was he even listening?

228
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:36,797
Son of a...

229
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,880
of course I'm going to follow him!

230
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:40,680
I'm coming with you, dammit!

231
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:44,900
There's no way!

232
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,177
What on earth is that police thinking?

233
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:50,025
Not only jumping ahead,
but changing cars, too!

234
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,657
You've got to be kidding me!

235
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:53,437
Does he mean to skip
the watering holes and

236
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:56,197
cut straight through the
middle of the desert?

237
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:57,880
Are you insane, Gyro?

238
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:00,500
We have 750 miles of sand ahead of us!

239
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,111
Do you have a death wish?

240
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:05,337
Better not forget, we're still
rivals in this race, you know?

241
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:07,157
I'm taking the quickest route.

242
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,711
Tag along if you want to.

243
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,475
Not much of a choice.

244
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,537
Somebody will take this shortcut.

245
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,855
Bet you Sandman will be right at home.

246
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,260
Damn it!

247
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:17,870
Man alive!

248
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:21,117
Jairo's not the only one
yelling to a certain death!

249
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,480
We've got a handful!

250
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:26,197
I don't think anyone in their
right mind would take this route!

251
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:28,868
It's like they're trying
to kill themselves!

252
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:48,357
We must bid our intrepid racers farewell
for the moment, ladies and gents.

253
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:53,322
We'll forge ahead as the railway decrees
and await their arrival at the checkpoint.

254
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:59,029
What's with that guy, huh?

255
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,337
Something's hanging from his ears,

256
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:04,297
but he's kicking up so much
sand I can't really see.

257
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:08,237
